  "notes": "Retroactive inoperability discovery: the Feb 3, 2020 trip investigation revealed a prior Nov 1, 2019 trip where the relay was degraded but passed testing due to inadequate procedure, extending the inoperability period back to Nov 1, 2019. CGMC A is mentioned only as concurrently inoperable during surveillance testing (contributing to loss-of-safety-function reportability), not as a failed component in the causal chain, so no FailureMode was created for it. No previous similar events per narrative. No backup system stated as operable during the inoperability window (Hydrogen Recombiners/Containment Spray/Venting discussed only in PRA risk-context, not as an operable backup during the event), so no BACKED_UP_BY edge per rule 6."
